<title>FRANCE: Algeria's packaging firm lost $13 mln in 1996.</title>
<headline>Algeria's packaging firm lost $13 mln in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Algeria's state-owned packaging firm, Entreprise Nationale des Emballages en Papier et Carton (ENEPAC), made a 777.41 million dinars ($13.8 million) loss in 1996, said the official Algerian news agency APS on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The ENEPAC posted a 7.4 billion dinars ($132.8 million) turnover in 1996, said APS without giving comparative figures.</p>
